      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_008"
      ],
      "explanation": "Work from the inside outward, using \\(|u|=-u\\) whenever \\(u<0\\). Since \\(x<-2\\), we have \\(1+x<-1<0\\), so\n\\[\n|1+x|=-(1+x)=-1-x.\n\\]\nIt follows that\n\\[\n1-|1+x|=1-(-1-x)=2+x.\n\\]\nThe condition \\(x<-2\\) also gives \\(2+x<0\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\bigl|1-|1+x|\\bigr|=|2+x|=-(2+x)=-2-x.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(-2-x\\), choice B.",
      "id": "inside-out-absolute-values",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1974_AMC_12_Q15#inside-out-absolute-values",
      "title": "Determine signs from the inside outward"
    }
  ],
